course: dictionary
lesson: 14517
title: Noticing small changes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how easy something is to notice. «Perceptibly» means in a way that you can notice or see, even if only a little. «The soup grew perceptibly colder.» You did not need a thermometer to know it: you could feel the change, so it was a change you could notice.
explain: Look at the words around it. Change words like colder, louder and faster show that something is changing, and perceptibly tells you how clearly you can notice the change. Try the check: swap in "you could notice it" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The opposite is imperceptibly, which means so slowly or slightly that you cannot notice it. «The hill rose imperceptibly, so we did not feel ourselves climbing.» Perceptibly and imperceptibly are a pair: one is noticeable, and the other is not.
fact: Perceptibly means in a way that can be noticed, even if only a little.
fact: «It grew perceptibly colder» means you could feel the change happening.
fact: Perceptibly often goes with change words such as colder, louder and faster.
fact: Imperceptibly is the opposite: so slight or slow that you cannot notice it.
fact: Perceptibly is often used in formal writing, science reports and stories.
exercise: «The train slowed perceptibly as it reached the station.» What does perceptibly mean here? | Without any reason | Very quickly and loudly | In a way nobody could ever see | *In a way you can notice
exercise: «The river rose imperceptibly all night, and nobody noticed until morning.» What does imperceptibly mean? | Very loudly and quickly | Clearly and brightly | *So slowly you cannot notice it
exercise: «The water became ___ warmer as the sun came out.» Which word fits best in the gap? | loudly | *perceptibly | sadly | happily
test: «The music grew perceptibly louder as the crowd cheered.» What does perceptibly mean? | Not at all | Very quietly | Slowly and sadly | *In a way you can notice, even a little
test: Jayden says, «The lift moved imperceptibly, so we felt nothing.» What does imperceptibly mean? | Clearly and with a big bang | Very fast and loud | Happily | *So slightly you cannot notice it
exam: Which sentence uses perceptibly correctly? | The sock was perceptibly blue. | *The kettle grew perceptibly hotter as we waited. | The kettle perceptibly sang a sad song. | We ate perceptibly for lunch.
